WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.503
-Our next guest is a talented
actress you know from

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.471
movies such as "Three Billboards
Outside Ebbing, Missouri,"

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:06.639
and "Ready or Not,"

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.541
as well as shows like
"Nine Perfect Strangers.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.044
She stars in "The Valet,"
which is streaming now on Hulu.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.244
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:13.579
-It's my publicist.

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:14.980
She's worried you're going to
say something stupid.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.549
-Me too.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.818
I'm nervous. Very nervous.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.220
I'm sweating. Look.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.720
-Oh, Jesus.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.890
Okay, well, can you talk to him
and tell him to stop sweating?

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:27.493
-Hello. I'm Antonio.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.062
-Just try not to say anything.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.097
They'll mostly
be focused on Olivia.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.132
-No, no, I-I don't want to
say anything.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.168
-But if you have to,
just say something like

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.170
you're here to support Olivia
on her big night.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.638
-Here to support Olivia
on her big night. Okay.

00:00:39.638 --> 00:00:41.340
-Oh, no.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.877
-Please welcome to the show
Samara Weaving, everyone!

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.047
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.897
Hi.
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.164
-I'm very happy to be here.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:08.267
-You play a very jaded actress
in this film.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.004
And for the premise -- I feel
like people should know it --

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.773
you have a secret relationship
with a billionaire

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.475
and you are trying to pass off
that you actually

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:18.745
have a relationship with this
valet, who was in that clip,

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.146
who was photographed in the back
with the two of you.

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:24.517
-Yes. We're trying to
pull one over the world

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.352
and hide our relationship.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.353
-You play a jaded actress,

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.989
but you are not yourself
a jaded actress.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.891
You are still capable of
being star-struck.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.159
-Yeah, not yet.
-Okay. That's good.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.994
-Not yet.
-I hope you get there one day.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.063
-Oh, I can't wait.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.098
-But I do think -- Like, I feel
the same way about --

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.767
There's still people I meet that
I get super-excited,

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.936
like a fan,
to see them in person.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.739
-Look, it's happening right now.
-Really? For me?

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.174
-Oh, yes.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:52.411
Every single human being that's
anything, I'm very sweaty.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:53.646
-Oh, okay.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.081
I feel like I was --
First, I was

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.315
really excited you said that,
and then you said,

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:57.350
"Every human being
who's anything."

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.718
-Oh, I'm so sorry!
[ Laughs ]

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:02.622
-It happens for literally any
human being.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:03.690
-Yeah.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.158
-If they have a pulse, I'm like,

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.959
"I can't believe
I'm meeting you."

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:08.227
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:11.364
I saw a Man with a Sign from
Instagram yesterday.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.600
-You saw a Man with a Sign?
-I saw a Man with a Sign.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.569
-Congratulations!
-I know.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.304
-Where did that happen?

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.872
-One of the streets.

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.040
-Oh, I see.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.742
You don't want to give away
any of the hints.

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:25.678
-Yeah, no.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.514
-Did you base -- Since you are
not a jaded actress,

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.850
did you base your character
on anyone?

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.552
-I like that you're
driving that home.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:38.257
You know, I based it on sort of
1920s Old Hollywood actresses.

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:39.559
-Alright.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:42.328
I read a story
where there was one actress

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.031
who refused to work
with babies or children

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:49.102
because they would steal
screen time from her.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.503
-That's very smart.
-Yeah.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.238
-They're also awful to work
with, so, yeah.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.372
-Well...
-Yeah.

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.875
You -- Paparazzi is
a big part of this film.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:59.311
Have you had problems with that
either here or in Australia?

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:00.445
-I mean, not really.

00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:05.217
You know, but in England,

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.420
when I lived there, they're
a bit -- they're intense.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.988
-I think they're known
for their intensity.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:14.394
-Sure. And I was having coffee
with my dad one day,

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.061
and they took photos of us.

00:03:16.061 --> 00:03:17.363
And the headline was like,

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.433
"Samara Weaving
seen with older gentleman."

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:24.403
That's a bit uncomfortable,
isn't it?

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:26.972
-That is a bit uncomfortable,
especially if your dad

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:28.174
didn't see the pictures,
and he's like,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.242
"Who's this older gentleman?"

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.176
-I think he was
maybe a bit excited.

00:03:31.176 --> 00:03:32.345
-Yeah. He got a little --

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.413
-He was like,
"I'm in the newspaper."

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.080
-Yeah. Your parents are
very supportive.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.349
-Yeah.
-I think that's always nice.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.919
Probably why you're not jaded.
-Perhaps.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.087
-They have helped you
over the years

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.888
with things like auditions?

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.757
-Yes. Yes, they have.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:48.193
-Is this true that they --
So, you know, when I say --

00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:50.096
For people who don't know,
sometimes, you have to send in

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.764
tape of yourself for a role.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.799
and you need somebody to
read the off-camera --

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:54.933
-Yeah, you need a reader,

00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:58.070
usually, like,
a friend or another actor.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.806
But, yeah, this one --
this one time --

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:04.810
I auditioned for "50 Shades of
Grey" in Los Angeles.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.813
And I went back to Australia,
and my parents had a house

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:10.449
at the time in this remote
part of Australia

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:11.450
called Broulee.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.453
About five people live there.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:17.356
And my agent called me and said,
"You've got a callback."

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:18.992
And I was thrilled

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.926
and then filled with dread,

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:26.031
because the only readers in
the house was my mum or my dad.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:29.669
And the scene was like,
"You did what where?"

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.538
And so I was like, "Oh, gosh.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:35.007
Okay, mum, do you mind just,
like -- Just look at the wall.

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.276
Don't look at me.

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:40.145
Just read these
very salacious lines,

00:04:40.145 --> 00:04:42.148
and I'll try my best.

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.384
It's a callback, okay?"

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:47.486
And she just stared at me
and was like,

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:50.255
"What are you doing
with your face?"

00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:51.424
-Oh, no.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:54.560
Your mom saw your
"50 Shades of Grey" face?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.629
-Yeah, she did.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.163
It's very traumatic.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.598
-Have things been
the same since?

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.867
-Well, it gets worse.
-Okay.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:04.136
-Because I fired mum.
I said, "You're out."

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:06.005
-Look, if you can't do the job,
you're gone.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:10.109
-You're done.
So I was like...

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.644
"Dad?"

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:18.918
And -- Ugh.
Look, it wasn't great.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:22.455
He got really into it.
-Yeah.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:25.557
Now, correct me if I'm wrong.
He actually did get cast, right?

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:27.726
He's in the film?
-He's in the movie.

00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:30.696
He's also known as Dakota.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.165
-He's the dignified
older gentleman in

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:34.199
"50 Shades of Grey."

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:37.803
-Yeah. Oh, gosh.
Look, I didn't get it.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:40.672
And that's fine.
-Yeah. It's fine.

00:05:40.672 --> 00:05:45.210
You have been
in some wonderful horror films.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.779
Are you a fan of horror?

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:47.880
-No.
-Okay.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.282
-No. I like the '80s ones,

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:52.051
the ones where you see
the strings.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.852
-Okay. Oh, I see.
-I don't know what this is.

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:55.287
-Those are strings, yeah.

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:56.689
So you don't like
how good the --

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.825
at this point,
the CGI is too good.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:05:59.925
It's too believable.
-It's too good.

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:02.227
Jump scares -- forget about it.

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:03.562
-So, your husband
actually filmed you,

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:04.964
and you were kind of enough
to -- This is maybe --

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:07.333
I've watched this like
five times today.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.369
This is a very genuine reaction.

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.270
-I look really incredible
in this clip.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.471
-You do look --
Thank you for getting

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:13.572
hair and makeup for this clip.

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:15.674
-I look like a worm.

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:18.878
-So this is -- You're
watching -- Is the film "It"?

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.379
-The opening of "It."
Couldn't make it.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:21.447
-The opening of "It."

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:24.150
And this is just
a genuine reaction to it.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.484
-Yeah, he filmed me,
and I didn't realize.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.319
You'll know why I didn't realize
he was filming me,

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:28.821
because I look fantastic.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:32.091
-You -- I just want to say,
I thought "It" was wonderful.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.259
I think this is
a little bit better.

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:36.962
The film of you watching "It"
might be better than "It."

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:38.363
Let's take a look real quick.

00:06:38.363 --> 00:06:39.699
-Oh.

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:48.674
Oh, no!

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:59.485
-That is -- I dare anybody to
show me something

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:02.822
more real in a
film or television show.

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:04.923
-It got animalistic.
It was guttural.

00:07:04.923 --> 00:07:07.059
Limbic system firing off.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.628
-Thank you for sharing it and
thanks for being here.

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:10.730
It's really such
a delight to meet you.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:11.864
-Thank you!

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:13.732
-You guys,
that's Samara Weaving.

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:17.569
"The Valet"
is streaming now on Hulu.

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:18.704
We'll be right back.

